To implement a multi-hop query in the LogQueryService class, you can modify the `fetchRelatedLogs` method as follows:

```java
public List<LogEntry> fetchRelatedLogs(String logId) {
    // Assuming a function getRelatedLogIds that retrieves related log IDs based on the current log ID
    List<String> relatedLogIds = getRelatedLogIds(logId);
    List<LogEntry> relatedLogs = new ArrayList<>();

    for (String relatedLogId : relatedLogIds) {
        LogEntry logEntry = logRepository.findById(relatedLogId);
        if (logEntry != null) {
            relatedLogs.add(logEntry);
        }
    }

    return relatedLogs;
}
```

Don't forget to update the `LogProcessor` to handle the incoming multi-hop query requests appropriately. After implementing, ensure to run `mvn test` to validate the changes.
